1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,130
Host: Welcome to KC desk note. Today we are unpacking one fresh research report and the question it raises.

2
00:00:06,490 --> 00:00:18,286
Host: Welcome back to the show. Today we’re diving into NIO’s first quarter 2026 results. The headline numbers look solid—revenue up 112% year on year.

3
00:00:18,646 --> 00:00:26,819
Host: But what really stands out is that they posted a second consecutive quarter of non-GAAP profit. So, what’s the real story here?

4
00:00:27,179 --> 00:00:32,520
Guest: That’s exactly the key frame. NIO delivered a strong quarter with revenue at the high end of guidance.

5
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:41,750
Guest: But the sequential drop from Q4 is expected—it’s a seasonal weak period. The more important takeaway is the margin improvement and the path to profitability.

6
00:00:42,110 --> 00:00:44,664
Host: So the market was watching for margins. What did we see?

7
00:00:45,024 --> 00:00:54,591
Guest: Gross margin hit 19%, up 11. 4 percentage points year on year and 1. 5 points sequentially. Vehicle margin was 18. 8%.

8
00:00:54,951 --> 00:01:03,310
Guest: That’s driven by a richer product mix—especially the ES8, which made up 54% of sales in Q1. Higher ASPs helped offset the volume dip.

9
00:01:03,670 --> 00:01:08,082
Host: And the profit picture—they still reported a net loss, but it’s shrinking fast.

10
00:01:08,442 --> 00:01:17,962
Guest: Right. Net loss narrowed 93% year on year to just under 500 million yuan. And on a non-GAAP basis, they were profitable for the second quarter in a row.

11
00:01:18,322 --> 00:01:25,566
Guest: That’s a big milestone. Operating margin was minus 1. 2%, but that’s a massive improvement from minus 53% a year ago.

12
00:01:25,926 --> 00:01:29,688
Host: So they’re getting closer to breakeven. But what about the outlook for Q2?

13
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:39,986
Guest: Guidance is for 110 to 115 thousand deliveries, up over 50% year on year. Revenue is expected between 32. 8 and 34. 4 billion yuan.

14
00:01:40,346 --> 00:01:47,591
Guest: That implies ASP might dip slightly to around 267k, because newer models like the Onvo L80 and the upcoming ES9 could shift the mix.

15
00:01:47,951 --> 00:01:51,620
Host: The ES9 launch is next Wednesday. That seems like a big catalyst.

16
00:01:51,980 --> 00:02:00,153
Guest: Absolutely. The report highlights that pre-order data is positive, based on industry surveys. And management noted that with ES9 in stores,

17
00:02:00,513 --> 00:02:09,244
Guest: foot traffic has increased, which also helped ES8 orders. In fact, the first 20 days of May saw the highest ES8 order volume since October last year.

18
00:02:09,604 --> 00:02:13,830
Host: So the new model is pulling in customers for the whole brand. That’s a nice halo effect.

19
00:02:14,190 --> 00:02:23,431
Guest: Exactly. But there are headwinds too. Management flagged that input costs—like lithium, memory, aluminum, and copper—are rising. The impact is about 10,

20
00:02:23,791 --> 00:02:33,079
Guest: 000 yuan per vehicle, but it hasn’t fully hit Q1 results due to inventory. They still target vehicle gross margins of 17 to 18 percent for Q2 and the full year.

21
00:02:33,439 --> 00:02:41,798
Host: That’s a key risk to watch. So the report is bullish, but it doesn’t settle everything. What’s one thing the full report dives into that we’re skipping here?

22
00:02:42,158 --> 00:02:51,493
Guest: One area is the detailed cost structure—R&D spending, SG&A targets, and the chip penetration plans for their self-developed Shenji NX9031.

23
00:02:51,853 --> 00:02:57,193
Guest: The report has a lot of granularity on how they plan to control costs while scaling. That’s worth reading closely.

24
00:02:57,553 --> 00:03:07,770
Host: And the analyst maintains a research view rating with an USD 8. 6 target price. The stock trades at about 0. 7 times forward sales.

25
00:03:08,130 --> 00:03:10,777
Host: That seems reasonable if the margin story holds.

26
00:03:11,137 --> 00:03:20,379
Guest: It does. But the real debate is whether NIO can sustain this momentum as competition heats up and costs rise. The report leaves that open for discussion.

27
00:03:20,739 --> 00:03:22,318
Host: Great. We’ll leave it there for now.

28
00:03:22,678 --> 00:03:31,223
Host: If you want to dig into the full report—especially the cost breakdown and margin assumptions—join the community conversation. Thanks for listening.

29
00:03:31,583 --> 00:03:32,790
Guest: Thanks for having me.
